{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenCoven/coven-cave/pulls/6050","id":4906988231,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSsT04M8AAAABJHqyxw","html_url":"https://github.com/OpenCoven/coven-cave/pull/6050","diff_url":"https://github.com/OpenCoven/coven-cave/pull/6050.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OpenCoven/coven-cave/pull/6050.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OpenCoven/coven-cave/issues/6050","number":6050,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Preserve tool lifecycle states and qualify activity disclosure","user":{"login":"BunsDev","id":68980965,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4OTgwOTY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68980965?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev","html_url":"https://github.com/BunsDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BunsDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nPreserve approval requests, cancellation requests, confirmed cancellation, and policy/user rejection as distinct tool observations. Qualify activity disclosure through live delivery, replay, raw transcript storage, ordinary logs, Client v1 reads, and HFR export.\n\n## Why\n\nRefs #5762. These states previously decoded as unknown or collapsed into an unspecified rejection. The issue also lacked a criterion-to-test map and explicit Client v1/export sentinel evidence.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Extend the additive display state model, validators, tracker request observations, labels, and first-terminal-wins fold. Requests never imply permission or confirmed effects.\n- Add lifecycle serialization/replay/settlement fixtures and forged receipt markers, including a proposal-review permit, to the real send-route disclosure fixture.\n- Check raw persisted JSON as well as projected history, authenticated Client v1 response bytes, and HFR JSONL.\n- Map all twelve original criteria to tests and document the remaining producer decision under OpenCoven/coven#1137.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused lifecycle, reasoning, correlation, migration, disclosure, export, and actual route tests pass.\n- Typecheck, full lint, test-registry validation (2,074 files), and diff checks pass.\n- All 1,442 app files pass across the original run and registry continuations (465 + 786 + 191). Initial interruptions were scratch-home overrides conflicting with fixtures; continuations preserve the existing assertions and runner flags with isolated storage.\n- All 517 API files pass across retry and continuation (347 + 170). The initial runs exposed fixture-home/socket-path assumptions under the isolation overrides; no assertions were changed.\n\n## Risk + rollout notes\n\nThis is an additive display contract. Existing adapters do not gain unsupported approval/cancellation capabilities. Legacy rejection retains its unspecified cause; disconnect/turn stop still means unknown, never confirmed cancellation. Binding, approval and effect references remain unavailable pending Val’s producer-contract decision. This PR does not close #5762 or claim native/provider/UI qualification owned by the downstream issues.\n\nCoven-Harness: codex / gpt-6\n","created_at":"2026-10-18T06:36:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T06:36:50Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ffb8a7da138dfbdabbc51dbb7125e2575d6b16f1","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.g